monte-hermoso-tree-analysis
===========================

Origin
------
The idea and the initial design of this project come from the Omdena
"Cordoba, Argentina Chapter" project, "Change Detection in Satellite Imagery:
Monitoring Land Use Transformation in Cordoba, Argentina":
https://github.com/OmdenaAI/CordobaArgentinaChapter_MonitoringLandUseTransformation

No files from that repository are included here; the code in this repository
was written for Monte Hermoso.

Data sources
------------
Data are read at runtime from Google Earth Engine and are not redistributed in
this repository, except the municipality boundary (data/aoi/monte_hermoso.geojson).

- Sentinel-2 SR Harmonized (COPERNICUS/S2_SR_HARMONIZED): Copernicus Sentinel
  Data Terms and Conditions. "Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data".
- Landsat Collection 2 Level-2 (Landsat 5/7/8/9): U.S. Geological Survey, public
  domain. Landsat imagery courtesy of the U.S. Geological Survey.
- Dynamic World v1 (GOOGLE/DYNAMICWORLD/V1): CC BY 4.0. Produced for the Dynamic
  World Project by Google in partnership with National Geographic Society and
  World Resources Institute. Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data.
  Brown, C.F., Brumby, S.P., Guzder-Williams, B. et al. Dynamic World, Near
  real-time global 10 m land use land cover mapping. Sci Data 9, 251 (2022).
  https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-022-01307-4
- Cloud Score+ S2_HARMONIZED (GOOGLE/CLOUD_SCORE_PLUS/V1/S2_HARMONIZED): CC BY 4.0.
  Pasquarella, V. J., Brown, C. F., Czerwinski, W., Rucklidge, W. J. (2023).
  Comprehensive Quality Assessment of Optical Satellite Imagery Using Weakly
  Supervised Video Learning. CVPR Workshops, 2125-2135.
  https://doi.org/10.1109/CVPRW59228.2023.00206
- Hansen Global Forest Change (UMD/hansen/global_forest_change_2025_v1_13): CC BY 4.0.
  Hansen, M. C. et al. (2013). High-Resolution Global Maps of 21st-Century Forest
  Cover Change. Science 342, 850-853. https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1244693
- MapBiomas Argentina Collection 3 (projects/mapbiomas-public/assets/argentina/lulc/collection3/...):
  CC BY 4.0, as stated on https://argentina.mapbiomas.org/descargas/mapas-de-la-coleccion/ .
  This repository does not redistribute MapBiomas layers. Project MapBiomas
  Argentina - Collection 3 of the Annual Land Cover and Land Use Maps of
  Argentina, accessed in 2026 through https://argentina.mapbiomas.org
- MapBiomas Pampa Collection 4 (projects/mapbiomas-public/assets/pampa/collection4/...):
  used only for the earlier comparison to 2023, under the MapBiomas terms of use
  (https://pampa.mapbiomas.org/en/terms-of-use/), which state a CC BY-SA license;
  other MapBiomas pages state CC BY 4.0. Not redistributed. Project MapBiomas
  Trinational Pampa - Collection 4 of the Annual Land Cover and Land Use Maps in
  Trinational Pampa, accessed in 2026 through https://pampa.mapbiomas.org
- CHIRPS Daily (UCSB-CHG/CHIRPS/DAILY): public domain (copyright waived).
  Funk, C. et al. (2015). The climate hazards infrared precipitation with
  stations - a new environmental record for monitoring extremes. Scientific
  Data 2, 150066. https://doi.org/10.1038/sdata.2015.66
- LandTrendr (ee.Algorithms.TemporalSegmentation.LandTrendr, parameters from
  github.com/eMapR/LT-GEE, Apache-2.0). Kennedy, R. E., Yang, Z., Cohen, W. B.
  (2010). Detecting trends in forest disturbance and recovery using yearly
  Landsat time series: 1. LandTrendr - Temporal segmentation algorithms.
  Remote Sensing of Environment 114, 2897-2910. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.rse.2010.07.008
- OpenStreetMap (nominatim.openstreetmap.org, accessed 2026): © OpenStreetMap
  contributors, ODbL (https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright). Used to locate
  places listed in data/reference/lugares_osm.csv and as the base map of
  docs/index.html. Street-end coordinates from OpenStreetMap also define two
  rectangles in data/reference/desarrollos_poligonos.geojson (Bungalow, Las
  Dunas). No other OpenStreetMap data is redistributed.
- Parcel 1050c outline in data/reference/desarrollos_poligonos.geojson: traced from
  the municipal zoning map (Plano_Zonificacion.pdf, Plan y Código de Ordenamiento
  Urbano y Territorial, Ord. 3246/2023, montehermoso.gov.ar) and georeferenced
  against the OpenStreetMap outline of Laguna Sauce Grande (ODbL). Approximate.
- Monte Hermoso del Este sector boundaries (data/reference/desarrollos_poligonos.geojson):
  taken from the public map linked from https://montehermosodeleste.com.ar
  (Google My Maps mid=1R3oPGHZZi7LAdVFMrDoY-DIc5OnEQL8). No license is stated by the
  publisher; they are used as a location reference only. Remove them if the
  publisher objects.
- Municipality boundary: IGN Argentina, via Georef (datos.gob.ar), CC BY 4.0.
  Servicio Georef - https://www.argentina.gob.ar/georef . The file in
  data/aoi/ is modified: the fields area_km2, source and source_date were added.
